Usages:
  collection_namespacing: |
    Every key-value store instance is scoped by a collection string supplied at construction.
    Two stores with different collection names never see each other's keys, even if a caller
    reuses the same key string across both. Choose a collection name unique to the owning
    subsystem.
  codable_value_encoding: |
    Non-primitive values are persisted by encoding to raw bytes (JSON for structured values,
    keyed archiving for secure-codable values) before the underlying write; reads reverse
    the same encoding. Callers never see the encoded representation directly.

Annotations: |
  This cell provides the lowest-level, non-domain-specific persistence primitives shared by
  every other subsystem: a namespaced key-value store and the GRDB-backed storage engine
  underneath the app's single on-disk database, plus the base protocols every persisted
  domain record conforms to.
  Use `collection_namespacing` and `codable_value_encoding` for `KeyValueStore`.

---

"KeyValueStore(collection: String)":
  location: KeyValueStore.swift
  annotations: |
    Namespaced key-value persistence wrapper used pervasively for simple settings/state.

    `collection`: the namespace this store's keys live in

    Use `collection_namespacing` for construction semantics.
    Use `codable_value_encoding` for any get/set of a non-primitive value.
  methods:
    "hasValue(key: String, transaction: DBReadTransaction) -> exists: Bool": |
      Returns whether a value is currently stored for `key`.
    "getString(key: String, transaction: DBReadTransaction) -> value: String?": |
      Returns the stored string for `key`, or nil if absent.
    "setString(value: String?, key: String, transaction: DBWriteTransaction)": |
      Stores `value` under `key`, or removes the key when `value` is nil.
    "getData(key: String, transaction: DBReadTransaction) -> value: Data?": |
      Returns the raw stored bytes for `key`.
    "setCodableValue(value: String, key: String, transaction: DBWriteTransaction)": |
      Encodes an arbitrary structured value and stores it under `key`.

      Use `codable_value_encoding` for the encode step.
    "getCodableValue(key: String, transaction: DBReadTransaction) -> value: String?": |
      Decodes and returns the structured value previously stored under `key`, or nil if absent.

      Use `codable_value_encoding` for the decode step.
    "removeValue(key: String, transaction: DBWriteTransaction)": |
      Deletes the value stored under `key`, if any.
    "allKeys(transaction: DBReadTransaction) -> keys: [String]": |
      Returns every key currently present in this store's collection.

"GRDBDatabaseStorageAdapter()":
  location: GRDBDatabaseStorageAdapter.swift
  annotations: |
    Lower-level SQLCipher/GRDB-backed storage engine wrapped by the cell-5 transaction facade.
    Owns the encrypted database file, connection pool, and directory-mode bookkeeping used
    during device transfer/restore.
  methods:
    "read(block: DBReadTransaction) -> result: String": |
      Opens a read transaction against the connection pool and runs `block` inside it.
    "writeWithTxCompletion(block: DBWriteTransaction) -> completion: String": |
      Opens a write transaction, runs `block`, and commits or rolls back per its returned
      completion value.
    "syncTruncatingCheckpoint()": |
      Forces a synchronous WAL checkpoint, truncating the write-ahead log file.

"DatabaseCorruptionState()":
  location: DatabaseCorruptionState.swift
  annotations: |
    Persists database-corruption status outside the database itself (in user defaults), so the
    corruption flag survives a subsequently rebuilt or deleted database file.
  properties:
    "status -> String": |
      One of: not corrupted, corrupted, or corrupted-but-already-dumped-and-restored.

"SDSModel()":
  location: SDSModel.swift
  annotations: |
    Protocol implemented by every persisted domain model (threads, interactions, jobs, and
    so on): declares the record's table name, its conversion to a storable record, and its
    insert operation. This is the base persistence contract the rest of the codebase's
    domain models build on.
  methods:
    "anyInsert(transaction: DBWriteTransaction)": |
      Inserts this model's current in-memory state as a new row.

"SDSRecord()":
  location: SDSRecord.swift
  annotations: |
    Protocol implemented by the GRDB-facing record counterpart of each `SDSModel` — the plain,
    directly-encodable/decodable row representation used for actual SQL fetch/persist calls.
  properties:
    "uniqueId -> String": |
      The stable identifier shared between a model and its record representation.

